      "properties": {
        "Node name for S&R": "MarkdownNote"
      },
      "widgets_values": [
        "## Qwen-Image-Layered -> Semantic Layers\n\n**Models** (into `ComfyUI/models/...`):\n- `diffusion_models/qwen_image_layered_bf16.safetensors`\n- `text_encoders/qwen_2.5_vl_7b_fp8_scaled.safetensors`\n- `vae/qwen_image_layered_vae.safetensors`\n\n**The decode chain that produces layers** \u2014 do not skip a step:\n`Empty Qwen Image Layered Latent` makes a 5-D latent `[B, 16, layers+1, H/8, W/8]`.\n`Latent Cut To Batch` with **dim = t** folds the layer axis into the batch axis.\n`VAE Decode` then returns ONE IMAGE batch of `layers+1` frames (RGB, no alpha).\n\n**Captions.** `Semantic Layer Analyze` is set to the `captions` analyzer, which needs one\ndescription per layer. Run once, open `Semantic Layer Debug` to see which layer is which,\nthen fill the captions box using the layer ids or indices it shows:\n\n    0 = blue sky and distant clouds\n    1 = a woman wearing a red jacket\n    2 = a wooden chair\n\nOr switch the analyzer to `florence2` to caption automatically (downloads weights), or\nwire any other captioner node's STRING output into the `captions` input.\n\n**Nothing here depends on layer order** \u2014 change `layers`, reorder them, and the seven\nrouter outputs keep the same meaning."
      ],
      "title": "Read me first"
    },
